(* Types of Hardness:) Tj
T*
(1. Temporary \(Carbonate\) Hardness: Caused by dissolved bicarbonates of calcium and) Tj
T*
(magnesium [Ca\(HCO3\)2, Mg\(HCO3\)2]. Readily precipitated by boiling:) Tj
T*
(Ca\(HCO3\)2 --[Heat]--> CaCO3 \(s\) + H2O + CO2 \(g\).) Tj
T*
(Mg\(HCO3\)2 --[Heat]--> Mg\(OH\)2 \(s\) + 2 CO2 \(g\).) Tj
T*
(2. Permanent \(Non-Carbonate\) Hardness: Caused by dissolved chlorides, sulfates, and) Tj
T*
(nitrates of calcium, magnesium, and heavy metals [CaCl2, MgCl2, CaSO4, MgSO4]. Cannot be) Tj
T*
(removed by boiling; requires chemical precipitation or ion exchange.) Tj
T*
(* Units of Hardness: Standardized to equivalent parts of Calcium Carbonate \(CaCO3,) Tj
T*
(Mol Wt = 100, Eq Wt = 50\):) Tj
T*
(- Parts per million \(ppm\): 1 ppm = 1 part of CaCO3 equivalent hardness per 10^6) Tj
T*
(parts of water.) Tj
T*
(- Milligrams per liter \(mg/L\): 1 mg/L = 1 mg of CaCO3 equivalent hardness per) Tj
T*
(liter of water. \(1 ppm = 1 mg/L\).) Tj
T*
(- Degree Clark \(deg Cl\): 1 part CaCO3 per 70,000 parts water. \(1 ppm = 0.07 deg) Tj
T*
(Cl\).) Tj
T*
(- Degree French \(deg Fr\): 1 part CaCO3 per 100,000 parts water. \(1 ppm = 0.10 deg) Tj
T*
(Fr\).) Tj
T*
(* Equivalence Formula:) Tj
T*
(CaCO3 equivalent = [ Mass of Hardness Substance \(mg/L\) * 50 ] / [ Equivalent Weight of) Tj
