(* Principle: Disodium salt of ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid \(Na2EDTA\) forms stable,) Tj
T*
(soluble 1:1 hexadentate chelate complexes with Ca2+ and Mg2+ ions at pH 10.0) Tj
T*
(\(buffered with NH4OH + NH4Cl\).) Tj
T*
(* Indicator: Eriochrome Black T \(EBT\). At pH 10, free EBT is blue. When added to hard) Tj
T*
(water, it binds a small fraction of metal ions forming an unstable wine-red complex:) Tj
T*
([M2+ + EBT] -> [M-EBT Complex] \(Wine Red\).) Tj
