T*
(* Scales and Sludges: Scales are hard, adherent, crystalline crusts \(CaSO4, CaCO3,) Tj
T*
(CaSiO3\) coating boiler tubes, causing localized overheating and tube blowout. Sludges) Tj
T*
(are soft, slimy, non-adherent precipitates \(MgCO3, MgCl2\) settling in low-flow areas.) Tj
T*
(* Caustic Embrittlement: In high-pressure boilers, residual Na2CO3 hydrolyzes: Na2CO3) Tj
T*
(+ H2O -> 2 NaOH + CO2. Concentrated NaOH penetrates hairline stress cracks in riveted) Tj
T*
(boiler joints, dissolving protective Fe3O4: Fe + 2 NaOH -> Na2FeO2 + H2. Leaves steel) Tj
T*
(brittle and prone to catastrophic failure. Prevented by adding sodium phosphate or) Tj
T*
(tannin.) Tj
T*
(* Priming and Foaming: Priming is carryover of water droplets in steam; Foaming is) Tj
T*
(persistent bubble formation on water surface caused by dissolved oils/organics.) Tj
T*
(Prevented by anti-foaming agents \(castor oil, polyamides\).) Tj
