T*
(* Zeolite / Permutit Process: Microporous hydrated sodium aluminosilicate) Tj
T*
(\(Na2O.Al2O3.xSiO2.yH2O, denoted Na2Ze\). Hard water percolates through zeolite bed:) Tj
T*
(Na2Ze + Ca\(HCO3\)2 -> CaZe + 2 NaHCO3; Na2Ze + MgSO4 -> MgZe + 2 Na2SO4.) Tj
T*
(Exhausted bed regenerated with 10% brine: CaZe + 2 NaCl -> Na2Ze + CaCl2 \(eluted to) Tj
T*
(drain\). Residual hardness: ~10-15 ppm. Cannot treat acidic or turbid water.) Tj
T*
(* Ion-Exchange \(Demineralization\) Process: Complete removal of all ions:) Tj
T*
(- Cation Exchanger \(RH+\): 2 RH + Ca2+ -> R2Ca + 2 H+. Regenerated with dilute) Tj
T*
(HCl/H2SO4.) Tj
T*
(- Anion Exchanger \(ROH-\): 2 R'OH + SO4^2- -> R'2SO4 + 2 OH-. Regenerated with) Tj
T*
(dilute NaOH.) Tj
T*
(- Effluent H+ and OH- neutralize: H+ + OH- -> H2O. Residual hardness: < 2 ppm) Tj
T*
(\(Deionized pure water\).) Tj
T*
(* Reverse Osmosis \(RO\): Applying hydrostatic pressure exceeding the osmotic pressure) Tj
T*
(\(Delta P > Pi\) across a semi-permeable thin-film composite membrane) Tj
T*
(\(polyamide/cellulose acetate\) forces pure water against the concentration gradient,) Tj
T*
(rejecting 99% of dissolved salts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
