(- Mg\(HCO3\)2: Mol Wt = 146, Eq Wt = 73. Factor = 50 / 73 = 100 / 146.) Tj
T*
(CaCO3 equivalent = 14.6 * \(50 / 73\) = 10.0 mg/L \(ppm\).) Tj
T*
(- CaSO4: Mol Wt = 136, Eq Wt = 68. Factor = 50 / 68 = 100 / 136.) Tj
T*
(CaCO3 equivalent = 13.6 * \(50 / 68\) = 10.0 mg/L \(ppm\).) Tj
T*
(- MgCl2: Mol Wt = 95, Eq Wt = 47.5. Factor = 50 / 47.5 = 100 / 95.) Tj
T*
(CaCO3 equivalent = 9.5 * \(50 / 47.5\) = 10.0 mg/L \(ppm\).) Tj
T*
(- MgSO4: Mol Wt = 120, Eq Wt = 60. Factor = 50 / 60 = 100 / 120.) Tj
T*
(CaCO3 equivalent = 12.0 * \(50 / 60\) = 10.0 mg/L \(ppm\).) Tj
T*
(- Note: NaCl and SiO2 do not cause hardness \(non-hardness impurities\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Temporary Hardness \(Sum of Bicarbonates\):) Tj
T*
(Temporary Hardness = Equivalent [ Ca\(HCO3\)2 + Mg\(HCO3\)2 ] = 10.0 + 10.0 = 20.0 ppm.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Permanent Hardness \(Sum of Sulfates and Chlorides\):) Tj
T*
(Permanent Hardness = Equivalent [ CaSO4 + MgCl2 + MgSO4 ] = 10.0 + 10.0 + 10.0 = 30.0) Tj
T*
(ppm.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Total Hardness:) Tj
T*
(Total Hardness = Temporary + Permanent = 20.0 + 30.0 = 50.0 ppm \(mg/L\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 5: Convert to Degree French \(1 ppm = 0.10 deg Fr\):) Tj
T*
(Total Hardness in deg Fr = 50.0 * 0.10 = 5.0 deg French.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Water sample has 20 ppm temporary, 30 ppm permanent, and 50 ppm total) Tj
T*
(hardness.) Tj
