([SOLVED PROBLEM 2: EDTA Titration Quantitative Analysis]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: 50 mL of standard hard water containing 1.0 mg of pure CaCO3 per mL required) Tj
T*
(20.0 mL of EDTA solution for titration. 100 mL of an unknown hard water sample required) Tj
T*
(30.0 mL of the same EDTA solution. 100 mL of the same water sample after boiling and) Tj
T*
(filtering required 10.0 mL of EDTA solution. Calculate: \(1\) Total hardness, \(2\)) Tj
T*
(Permanent hardness, \(3\) Temporary hardness in ppm.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Standardize EDTA Solution:) Tj
T*
(50 mL of standard water = 50 * 1.0 mg = 50.0 mg CaCO3 equivalent.) Tj
T*
(20.0 mL EDTA = 50.0 mg CaCO3 => 1.0 mL EDTA = 50.0 / 20.0 = 2.50 mg CaCO3 equivalent.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Total Hardness of Unknown Sample:) Tj
T*
(100 mL water required 30.0 mL EDTA = 30.0 * 2.50 = 75.0 mg CaCO3 equivalent.) Tj
T*
(In 1,000 mL \(1 Liter\) of water = 75.0 * \(1000 / 100\) = 750.0 mg/L.) Tj
T*
(Total Hardness = 750.0 ppm.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Permanent Hardness \(Boiled Water\):) Tj
T*
(100 mL boiled water required 10.0 mL EDTA = 10.0 * 2.50 = 25.0 mg CaCO3 equivalent.) Tj
T*
(In 1,000 mL of water = 25.0 * \(1000 / 100\) = 250.0 mg/L.) Tj
T*
(Permanent Hardness = 250.0 ppm.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Temporary Hardness:) Tj
T*
(Temporary Hardness = Total Hardness - Permanent Hardness = 750.0 - 250.0 = 500.0 ppm.) Tj
T*
(Final Results: Total = 750 ppm | Permanent = 250 ppm | Temporary = 500 ppm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
