(Problem: A zeolite water softener bed completely softened 40,000 liters of hard water) Tj
T*
(containing 350 ppm of total hardness before exhaustion. Calculate the mass of sodium) Tj
T*
(chloride \(NaCl\) in kilograms required to regenerate the exhausted zeolite bed using 10%) Tj
T*
(brine solution.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Total CaCO3 Equivalent Hardness Removed:) Tj
T*
(Total water volume = 40,000 Liters.) Tj
T*
(Hardness = 350 mg/L = 350 g / 1000 L.) Tj
T*
(Total CaCO3 hardness removed = 40,000 L * 350 mg/L = 14,000,000 mg = 14.0 kg CaCO3) Tj
T*
(equivalent.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Stoichiometric NaCl Regeneration Relationship:) Tj
T*
(Regeneration reaction: CaZe + 2 NaCl -> Na2Ze + CaCl2.) Tj
T*
(100 g CaCO3 equivalent requires 2 * 58.5 g = 117.0 g NaCl.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Calculate Required Mass of NaCl:) Tj
T*
(Mass of pure NaCl = [ Total CaCO3 equivalent \(kg\) * 117.0 ] / 100.0) Tj
T*
(Mass of NaCl = [ 14.0 kg * 117.0 ] / 100.0 = 16.38 kg of pure NaCl.) Tj
T*
(If commercial salt is 95% pure:) Tj
T*
(Commercial Salt Required = 16.38 / 0.95 = 17.24 kg.) Tj
