T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: Calculate the minimum theoretical hydrostatic pressure \(P_min\) required to) Tj
T*
(desalinate brackish water containing 5,850 mg/L of dissolved NaCl at 25 deg C \(298 K\)) Tj
T*
(via Reverse Osmosis. \(Van't Hoff factor i = 2 for NaCl; gas constant R = 0.0821) Tj
T*
(L*atm/mol*K\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute Molar Concentration of NaCl:) Tj
T*
(Molar mass of NaCl = 58.44 g/mol.) Tj
T*
(Concentration C = 5.850 g/L / 58.44 g/mol = 0.1001 mol/L.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Calculate Osmotic Pressure Pi via Van't Hoff Equation:) Tj
T*
(Pi = i * C * R * T) Tj
T*
(Pi = 2 * \(0.1001 mol/L\) * \(0.0821 L*atm/mol*K\) * \(298 K\)) Tj
T*
(Pi = 2 * 0.1001 * 24.4658 = 4.898 atm.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Convert to SI Units \(1 atm = 101,325 Pa = 1.01325 bar\):) Tj
T*
(Pi = 4.898 * 1.01325 bar = 4.96 bar ~ 5.0 bar.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: The applied hydrostatic pump pressure must strictly exceed 4.96 bar) Tj
T*
(\(typically operated at 15-20 bar in practice to maintain adequate permeate flux\).) Tj
