(Answer: EDTA \(ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid\) is a hexadentate chelating ligand) Tj
T*
(possessing two amino nitrogens and four carboxylate oxygens that wrap around metal) Tj
T*
(cations in a stable octahedral cage. The titration is conducted at pH 10.0 using) Tj
T*
(NH4Cl-NH4OH buffer to ensure complete deprotonation of EDTA to EDTA^4- while preventing) Tj
T*
(precipitation of Mg\(OH\)2. Eriochrome Black T \(EBT\) indicator is added, binding Ca2+/Mg2+) Tj
T*
(to form an unstable wine-red complex: M2+ + EBT -> [M-EBT] \(wine-red\). During titration,) Tj
T*
(free EDTA preferentially chelates free Ca2+ and Mg2+ to form colorless, highly stable) Tj
T*
([M-EDTA]^2- complexes \(formation constant log K_f ~ 10.7 for Ca\). At the equivalence) Tj
T*
(point, EDTA displaces EBT from the metal-indicator complex. Free, uncomplexed EBT is) Tj
T*
(liberated into the alkaline buffer, producing a sharp, irreversible transition from WINE) Tj
T*
(RED to SKY BLUE.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Compare Zeolite process with Ion-Exchange Demineralization process across) Tj
T*
(chemistry, residual hardness, and operational constraints.) Tj
T*
(Answer: \(1\) Chemistry: Zeolite uses inorganic hydrated sodium aluminosilicates \(Na2Ze\)) Tj
T*
(that exchange only cations \(Ca2+, Mg2+\) for Na+; anions remain in water. Ion-Exchange) Tj
T*
(uses separate synthetic organic polystyrene resins: cation resin \(R-SO3H\) exchanges all) Tj
T*
(cations for H+, and anion resin \(R-NMe3OH\) exchanges all anions for OH-. \(2\) Residual) Tj
T*
(Hardness: Zeolite leaves 10-15 ppm residual hardness; Ion-Exchange produces completely) Tj
T*
(demineralized water with < 2 ppm hardness \(electrical conductivity < 0.1 microS/cm\). \(3\)) Tj
T*
(Treated Water Composition: Zeolite water contains high NaHCO3, causing caustic) Tj
T*
(embrittlement in high-pressure boilers. Ion-Exchange effluent contains zero dissolved) Tj
T*
(solids. \(4\) Constraints: Zeolite cannot treat acidic or turbid water \(acids destroy the) Tj
T*
(aluminosilicate cage\); Ion-Exchange resins handle acidic feed streams safely.) Tj
T*
